mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Functional discipline experiments are an important part of medical education and an indispensable component of the “three fundamentals” training. Their purpose is to strengthen students' basic operational skills through experimental teaching, cultivate and instill a rigorous and pragmatic scientific attitude, inspire and guide scientific thinking, and maximize students' initiative and creativity.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
